1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,440
Okay. All right. We're in a series on the book of Revelation. Does everybody know that? Remember

2
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:17,420
that? Some are excited. Others are, you know, like me, maybe wrestling. Anyway, the groundwork

3
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:21,960
that we have laid for the book of Revelation so far is that it is not a puzzle to be decoded,

4
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:28,240
contrary to popular interpretations. It isn't even primarily about future events,

5
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:35,180
but it is about the revealing of Jesus Christ. It is about showing us who Jesus is presently

6
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:41,260
ruling and reigning on his throne. It is written to seven real churches in the first century in Asia

7
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:46,560
Minor. It is written to encourage them. And so if John, a pastor, was writing to encourage seven

8
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:52,720
churches who were struggling with persecution, who were wanting to give up, what hope would a book be

9
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:57,920
that's about 2,000 years in the future? So there's hope here in the midst of the suffering,

10
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:03,220
for these challenging churches. And the picture of Jesus on the throne is intended to challenge.

11
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:07,800
There are churches that he's writing to that are in rebellion, that aren't listening to, aren't being

12
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:12,180
faithful, aren't doing what Jesus says. And he's giving them the same image that is going to challenge

13
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:18,800
rebellious churches, wake up stagnant churches, and encourage struggling churches. And the primary

14
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:24,440
message, again, that accomplishes that is this image of Jesus on the throne. Daryl Johnson

15
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:29,820
has these two lines that I think are really helpful for setting the context of the book. Revelation

16
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:36,780
sets the present realities in light of the unseen realities of the future. And Revelation sets the

17
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:41,260
present realities in light of the unseen realities of the present. If you could throw up that image

18
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:48,300
from our series in the book of Ephesians, essentially what Daryl is getting at here is we live, the church

19
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:53,580
lives in this in-between state between Christ's kingdom being inaugurated, which we would say happened at the

20
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:58,800
ascension, which is a thing that we don't often preach about in the American church. You always hear about

21
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:05,500
Christ's death, his blood shed on the cross. Sometimes we talk about his resurrection. We rarely talk about

22
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:11,380
his ascension. And his ascension is part of the whole gospel. If he did not, if he raised but did not

23
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:17,320
ascend, then things would look differently. Jesus raised and ascended on into heaven on the throne. And

24
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:22,620
right now this present reality, we live in a world where Jesus is ruling and reigning on a throne in

25
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:28,120
heaven, but that kingdom has not yet been consummated. It has not yet fully come to earth. And we are in

26
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:34,180
this in-between. A lot of scholars call it this already and not yet. And so what Daryl is getting at is the

27
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:39,840
book of Revelation pulls back the curtain. We've been using the curtain as an illustration to show us what

28
00:02:39,840 --> 00:03:02,700
what the kingdom of heaven looks like currently in its present reality and how that impacts our reality, the more visible, tangible, physical reality. And it puts it in perspective for the future as well. Does that make sense? If it doesn't, I can't say it any better than Daryl Johnson, so we're stuck.

29
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:25,480
Let's pray again. Let's pray again. Okay. I need it. I need it. I don't know if you need it, but we all need it. Jesus, we thank you for this book that is confusing and hard to understand at times, but gives us and is intended to give us a clearer picture and image of what your kingdom looks like right now.

30
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:32,840
And oftentimes we're, we're so consumed by the tangible, visible things in front of us.

31
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:48,480
Help us to remember that we are not just physical beings, but we are spiritual beings and both the physical and the eternal come together in this book in Revelation. Give us eyes to see, ears to hear.

32
00:03:48,480 --> 00:04:16,020
And God, God, I pray that this book would be a book that encourages us to live faithfully in the midst of a broken world, that it wouldn't just be intellectual exercise that we think about, pontificate about this spiritual reality, but it would become a present thing in our hearts that changes the way that we live, that encourages us to love our neighbors and to endure persecution and to whatever obedience you call us to.

33
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:25,080
God, may this book, may this image of a slain lamb on a throne truly transform who we are as a people until you return.

34
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:27,520
It's in Jesus' name I pray. Amen.

35
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:36,140
So I heard one pastor say that if you were to poll Christians in America and ask them what book you most want at your church to preach on,

36
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:41,320
that most likely many Christians would answer the book of Revelation.

37
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:49,220
But if you were to poll most pastors in churches in America, what book would they most like to preach on?

38
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:54,100
And Revelation would probably be towards the bottom of that list.

39
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,620
It's hard work.

40
00:04:56,620 --> 00:04:58,200
It's heavy study.

41
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:08,140
And I think it's often because many congregants, and this is not anybody's fault other than maybe pop culture and one certain book series that we will not name,

42
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:15,000
has trained people to think that the book of Revelation is answering the question, when will these things happen?

43
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:23,220
And of course, like, if we're talking about tribulation and persecution and hardship, like, it would make sense for you to be in the room and say,

44
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:26,300
well, if we know this is coming, I'd like to know when and how it's coming.

45
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:26,800
Right?

46
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:29,940
It's a very pragmatic question to ask.

47
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:37,460
But I think pastors, one of the reasons there's this tension between congregants and pastors is many pastors know that that's really not the question,

48
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:40,740
and that the actual question is far less fun to answer.

49
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:49,260
Because the actual question that's being asked in the book of Revelation is, how do we remain faithful to Jesus as these things play out?

50
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,780
What does faithfulness look like?

51
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:59,340
In Revelation, it can become, and this is my pastoral frustration, it can become a book that Christians get obsessed with studying.

52
00:05:59,340 --> 00:06:05,740
And there can be this, like, we pat ourselves on the back because we're like, man, I'm really in the word.

53
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:10,820
But the way in which we study it does nothing to transform the way that we live in our everyday lives.

54
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:17,820
And so if you've found a way to study a book of the Bible where it does not confront you as a person in your obedience to Jesus,

55
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:22,800
then you're missing the point because the whole point of the Bible is to be conforming us into the image of Jesus.

56
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:31,580
So, if you are coming to the book of Revelation and you want to ask the question, when will these things happen?

57
00:06:31,580 --> 00:06:34,120
I want to put you at ease and tell you that you're in good company.

58
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:40,360
Because the 12 disciples, Jesus' closest followers, at the very end of their following him,

59
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:43,280
three years of just being with Jesus day in and day out.

60
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:46,880
Jesus finally brings up a little bit of eschatology in Matthew 24.

61
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:49,700
Eschatology just means end times, right?

62
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:55,000
He's talking a little bit about this time between when he's going to leave them and when he's going to come back.

63
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,780
And he tells them some things that sound hard.

64
00:06:57,780 --> 00:07:01,520
And do you want to know what the question that his disciples, his closest followers, ask him?

65
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:04,760
When will these things happen, right?

66
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,940
It's a good question.

67
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:08,760
Like, it's the question that all of us want to know.

68
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:13,860
And John, like Jesus, pretty much ignores that question altogether.

69
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:19,860
If you read Matthew 24 and 25 this week, you'll find out that Jesus pretty much just ignores the question.

70
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:23,260
Actually, the one answer that he gives to them is, no one knows.

71
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:27,640
AKA, don't waste your time trying to predict the future.

72
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:37,200
Instead, he opts to give them a message about not being afraid, not being deceived, to stay awake, to remain faithful to the kingdom of God.

73
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,260
And Revelation is really serving that same purpose.

74
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:53,600
John is giving these churches, and through these churches, us, apocalyptic images to meditate on that are intended not to give us clarity on when these things will take place,

75
00:07:53,600 --> 00:08:05,780
but to encourage us not to be afraid or deceived when and if they do, to remain faithful to God's kingdom even when the future is uncertain.

76
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:12,000
And another reason pastors don't really like to preach the book of Revelation is you probably wouldn't have known up to this point,

77
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,500
because we've been in chapters 1 through 5.

78
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:16,660
Everybody loves to preach chapters 1 through 5.

79
00:08:16,660 --> 00:08:20,980
And we're going to get to chapters 21 and 22.

80
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:24,580
Every pastor loves to preach Revelation chapter 21 and 22.

81
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:28,020
You know what, the reason pastors don't want to preach the book of Revelation?

82
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:32,220
Everything I already said in chapters 6 through 20.

83
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,000
So it's about to get weird is all I'm saying.

84
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:38,060
The weird things, if you're like, man, this hasn't been that bad.

85
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:39,040
It's been pretty nice so far.

86
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:39,680
Yes, it has.

87
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,360
Chapters 1 through 5 are pretty nice.

88
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:44,720
Chapters 21 and 22, pretty nice.

89
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:49,220
The middle, it's interesting, okay?

90
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:53,160
There's lots of symbolic numbers and images.

91
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:56,760
We're going to start today a set of seven.

92
00:08:56,860 --> 00:08:58,620
There's three sets of sevens coming up.

93
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:03,460
Seven seals, seven trumpets, seven bowls that go from chapter 6 to chapter 16.

94
00:09:04,280 --> 00:09:11,480
And what often happens is we read them like chronological events that have to take place, asking the question, when will these things happen?

95
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:14,580
Are we in the seven seals, the seven trumpets, the seven bowls?

96
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:24,000
And again, I just want us to try and step back from that question and instead receive them as apocalyptic images to be meditated on.

97
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,980
It's not about chronology.

98
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:34,720
And the best illustration that I could come up with this week as I was thinking about this is how many classical music fans do we have?

99
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:36,040
Yeah.

100
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:42,780
I knew that the few in here would be eager to raise their hands because that's a very humble brag.

101
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:45,280
Yep, me, I listen to classical music.

102
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:49,480
I have, and I enjoy it, but I'm not going to say it here.

103
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:54,640
Just like I'm wearing a messy jersey today, I am a capital B bandwagon fan.

104
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:59,180
I don't really watch that much football, soccer, however you want to say it.

105
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:04,060
I'm not going to claim to be a classical music fan, but, you know, I can hang.

106
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:04,980
I can hang.

107
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:16,980
And if we think about kind of one of the more famous, well-known classical pieces in our modern time, Beethoven's Fifth Symphony, he establishes this powerful melody.

108
00:10:16,980 --> 00:10:18,540
Anybody have it?

109
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:20,940
Give it to me.

110
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:26,900
See, I'm thankful somebody else did it to me, and then I still did it.

111
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:27,420
That's embarrassing.

112
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:27,780
All right.

113
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:33,820
He establishes this really clear, powerful melody, and it gets repeated, and it gets intensified.

114
00:10:33,820 --> 00:10:35,860
It gets brought to climactic crescendos.

115
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:42,840
You think the song is over, and then we go back, and we loop around, and we hit a similar melody from a different angle.

116
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:49,780
We're hearing things, seeing things that sound similar but are different, that all come together into one piece.

117
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:57,740
And I introduced that as an illustration because I think that really sets up the next section, the seven seals, the seven trumpets, the seven bowls.

118
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:12,100
Because I think they are similar images aimed at kind of drawing out the same ideas, the stirring our imagination, and shaping the way that we think about this time between Christ's ascension and Christ's return.

119
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:16,300
And what John doesn't want is the same thing that Beethoven didn't want.

120
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:28,600
Beethoven did not want you to stare at the score of his masterpiece and analyze every little detail, every little note, every little rest, every little crescendo.

121
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,560
He didn't want you to stare at the score.

122
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:34,380
He wanted you to sit back with your eyes closed and experience the music.

123
00:11:35,280 --> 00:11:40,260
And I think this is helpful for us because I think this is what John is doing with these images.

124
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:47,400
He's giving us images that are intended for us to not overanalyze and try and parse out every specific detail,

125
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:58,520
but he's trying to stir our emotions and ultimately shape our imagination about what it looks like to anchor our hope in the slain lamb who is sitting on the throne,

126
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:01,040
even when the future looks unknown.

127
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:06,880
So with the rest of our time, I'm going to hopefully give us these images in a way that we can meditate on them

128
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:12,160
and allow them to answer some questions for us that I think John did intend to answer.

129
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:18,220
Not the win question, but questions that have application for our everyday lives.

130
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:18,680
Sound good?

131
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:19,880
All right.

132
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:24,160
We have a lot of Scripture and I'm going to do my best.

133
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:26,400
So just give me grace.

134
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:26,720
Okay.

135
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,620
Revelation chapter six is where we're going to be.

136
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:34,940
And the first set of images that we're going to look at are famous in pop culture.

137
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:37,580
Anybody heard of the four horsemen of the apocalypse?

138
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:39,120
All right.

139
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,720
So that's the first set of images that we're going to look at.

140
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:44,680
It's in Revelation chapter six, verses one through eight.

141
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:48,860
And I think the question that these horsemen are going to answer for us,

142
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:52,520
if we just sit back and meditate on the images that they are,

143
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:56,840
I think they're going to answer for us the question, what kind of a world do we live in?

144
00:12:56,840 --> 00:13:04,440
What kind of a world do we live in between the ascension of Jesus and the second coming of Jesus,

145
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,380
this time between the inaugurated and consummated kingdom?

146
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:12,180
I think the horsemen are going to give us an image of what happens in human history.

147
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:19,360
Whether it's a, some people would argue that the four horsemen are an event that happened in the past when the temple was destroyed.

148
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:24,060
Some people will argue that it's a cyclical pattern of things that happen in the present.

149
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:27,600
Some people will argue that it is a future event that has not yet happened.

150
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:33,600
My argument is that to get stuck on the specifics of whether it's a past, present, or future event

151
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:39,080
is to miss the application that John wants us to get by meditating on the images.

152
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:39,780
Does that make sense?

153
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:40,800
All right.

154
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:48,940
So eventually you can get to the point where you can spend time thinking about what specifically you think is happening there.

155
00:13:48,940 --> 00:13:55,980
But my argument is that we don't have to really get there to allow it to shape our imagination and to stir our affections for Jesus.

156
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:56,940
Okay.

157
00:13:56,940 --> 00:14:01,440
So Revelation 6 verses 1 through 8.

158
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:16,060
So for context, so that we remember from Quarry's message, he hears a roaring lion and he sees a lamb, a little lamb, as if slain, who's sitting on the throne.

159
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:25,240
And then John sees a scroll, which pretty much all commentators would argue is the redemptive plan of God for human history.

160
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:28,860
And that redemptive plan of God through human history is sealed with seven seals.

161
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:37,660
And there's weeping in heaven because nobody is worthy to open the scroll except for the powerful, strong lion.

162
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:43,560
No, the lamb who has been slain, he is worthy to open the scroll.

163
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,480
So he takes the scroll.

164
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,420
He now is beginning to open it.

165
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:52,620
I watched the lamb open one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures say with a voice like thunder,

166
00:14:53,020 --> 00:15:04,060
come, and I looked, and behold, a white horse, and its rider had a bow and a crown was given to him, and he came out conquering to conquer.

167
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:11,620
When he opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature say, come, and out came another horse, bright red.

168
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:18,900
Its rider was permitted to take peace from the earth so that people should slay one another, and he was given a great sword.

169
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:27,180
And we opened the third seal, I heard the living creature say, come, and I looked, and behold, and a black horse and its rider had a pair of scales in his hand,

170
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:37,260
and I heard what seemed to be a voice in the midst of the four living creatures say, a quart of wheat for a denarius, and three quarts of barley for a denarius, and do not harm the oil and the wine.

171
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:47,500
And when he opened the fourth seal, I heard the fourth living creature say, come, and I looked, and behold, a pale horse, and its rider's name was Death,

172
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:58,320
and Hades followed him, and they were given authority over a fourth of the earth to kill with a sword, and with famine, and with pestilence, and with wild beasts on the earth.

173
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:01,080
And everyone said, praise be to God.

174
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:03,900
Right?

175
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:05,880
This is the word of the Lord.

176
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:09,540
The worthy lamb, as though slain, begins to open the seven seals.

177
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:12,320
What is happening?

178
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:19,280
Exposing the events that will take place between the inaugurated and consummated kingdom of God.

179
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:22,160
And the first four seals, the four horsemen, they all look different,

180
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:28,960
but I would argue they are prophetic images describing what the world is like between the already and not yet kingdom.

181
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:33,880
It's important context for us to know that John is not inventing these symbols out of nowhere.

182
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:38,540
These are symbols that had been repeated from the prophets in the Old Testament.

183
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:40,280
John didn't just make up something.

184
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:48,540
These are John joining in the symphony of the prophetic images of the Jewish and Christian people,

185
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:52,220
and he is expounding on them and bringing them forward.

186
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:53,500
So he's not making up images.

187
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:58,180
You can read all of these horses in Ezekiel and Isaiah and other prophets.

188
00:16:58,180 --> 00:17:04,300
I also want to note that each of the four seals begins with that,

189
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:06,560
and you heard me overemphasizing this.

190
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:13,100
Each of the four seals starts with a exclamation from one of the four living creatures where he says,

191
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:13,880
come.

192
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:20,440
And this can get confusing because it almost sounds like one of the four living creatures is inviting the four horsemen to come,

193
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:23,660
which seems scary, right?

194
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:27,320
Why would these people who are on Jesus's team bowing at his throne,

195
00:17:27,320 --> 00:17:31,540
why are they inviting this tribulation and persecution to come?

196
00:17:31,540 --> 00:17:33,960
But what I would argue, and I think is the better answer,

197
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:37,760
is that these creatures are praying for Jesus to come back.

198
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:40,460
They want Christ to come.

199
00:17:40,520 --> 00:17:41,760
They're saying, Christ, come.

200
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:43,300
Christ, come.

201
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:47,060
We see in Revelation chapter one, the book says that Jesus is coming,

202
00:17:47,060 --> 00:17:49,600
that he is present and actively on his way,

203
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:52,940
and all of creation is praying that Jesus would come.

204
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:55,840
But what has to happen before Jesus can come

205
00:17:55,840 --> 00:18:01,620
is that the enemy of God has to be released onto the world to deceive and lead astray.

206
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:05,560
And so these creatures are representatives of creation.

207
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:12,000
Four in Jewish numerology is just a number for kind of all four corners of the earth,

208
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,100
the four creatures, the four living creatures.

209
00:18:14,100 --> 00:18:15,800
They represent all of creation.

210
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:18,520
And I would argue that this is what we read in Romans chapter eight.

211
00:18:18,520 --> 00:18:23,240
This is an image of creation crying out, groaning for Christ to return.

212
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:29,000
All of creation is broken, and all of creation groans for Christ to return.

213
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,600
They pray for Christ to return.

214
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:34,580
But what has to happen before that is the horsemen get to ride.

215
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:39,980
And the first horse is how I would define it as a horse.

216
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:45,380
I get, yes, you're getting a segment of Baptist preaching for the next 10 minutes, okay?

217
00:18:45,380 --> 00:18:47,040
Four Ds.

218
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,600
Four Ds.

219
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,200
The first, deception.

220
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:54,960
The first horse resembles images of Jesus in the book of Revelation.

221
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:58,340
There are actually some scholars that would argue that the first horse is Jesus

222
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:02,820
because it's so similar to some of the other images of Jesus in Revelation.

223
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:07,020
We see Jesus on a white horse with a sword coming out of his mouth.

224
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:12,840
The problem is that Jesus is going to come on a white horse with a sword in his mouth,

225
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:15,900
and he's going to be covered in blood, and that blood is his own blood.

226
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:21,140
And this horse has a bow and is coming out to conquer.

227
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:23,320
And so he's trying to have victory.

228
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,040
Jesus lays down his life to have victory.

229
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,080
He doesn't need to use the sword.

230
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:33,180
The sword is coming out of his mouth because his gospel of truth is the thing that brings salvation and judgment.

231
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:36,940
His own blood is the thing that brings salvation and judgment.

232
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:42,140
This horse is riding to conquer, and it has a bow in its hand.

233
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:49,860
And again, let's think back to our series in Ephesians when Paul says that we should put on the armor of God.

234
00:19:49,860 --> 00:19:53,940
Christians put on the armor of God to distinguish the fiery what?

235
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:56,300
Arrows.

236
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,180
Of who?

237
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:58,540
The enemy.

238
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:03,160
Okay, so I would argue that this is deception.

239
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:07,400
This is the enemy proclaiming false Gospels to the people on earth.

240
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:14,780
It is the enemy trying to get us to put our hope in something that looks like Jesus but falls short every single time.

241
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:18,820
Jesus says, I am the way, the truth, and the life.

242
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:23,180
The enemy says, power is the way, the truth, and the life.

243
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:25,440
Wealth is the way, the truth, and the life.

244
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:27,460
Empire is the way, the truth, and the life.

245
00:20:27,460 --> 00:20:29,880
Tribalism is the way, the truth, and the life.

246
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:32,800
Progressive secularism is the way, the truth, and the life.

247
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:35,540
Democratic capitalism is the way, the truth, and the life.

248
00:20:35,540 --> 00:20:38,280
Insert whatever worldview or ideology you want.

249
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:43,160
The enemy will try and counterfeit the good news of Jesus with something less than Jesus.

250
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:47,620
And it is using that false gospel to try and conquer the people of the earth.

251
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:50,400
It imitates the message of Jesus.

252
00:20:50,400 --> 00:21:03,820
It says, you can have peace, you can have prosperity, you can have success, but all of it is temporary and short-sighted in light of the eternal kingdom of the Jesus who comes on a white horse with a sword out of his mouth covered in his own blood.

253
00:21:03,820 --> 00:21:05,980
This is the good news of Jesus.

254
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:14,900
The spiritual powers counterfeit the gospel and promise people peace through putting their hope and allegiance in something other than the lamb who sits on the throne.

255
00:21:14,900 --> 00:21:23,420
So, horse number one, false Gospels, deception, the enemy trying to get, and this is unleashed at Christ's ascension.

256
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:29,100
The enemy is trying to get people to reject the good news of Jesus for a false gospel.

257
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:32,540
It's already started in the seven churches in Asia Minor.

258
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:35,920
And John wants them to see, you're being deceived.

259
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:39,460
These arrows are aimed to kill you, not to give you life.

260
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:44,740
And when people believe false Gospels, the second horse rides.

261
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:46,620
The second horse is that of division.

262
00:21:46,620 --> 00:21:47,320
We saw it.

263
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,480
The horse is bright red.

264
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:51,500
It was permitted to take peace from the earth.

265
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,340
People begin to slay one another.

266
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:55,340
It's given a sword.

267
00:21:55,340 --> 00:21:57,180
And here's what happens.

268
00:21:57,180 --> 00:22:03,420
This is a, I would argue that this is a pattern of things that happen in society throughout human history.

269
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:12,280
When people are deceived and begin to believe a false gospel, a competing gospel, it pushes us into tribalism and a scarcity mindset.

270
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:21,780
If I believe the gospel of democratic capitalism and you believe the gospel of progressive secularism and socialism, then you and I are at odds.

271
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:28,660
We are in different tribes and we are all competing for a limited number of votes and resources and whatever.

272
00:22:28,660 --> 00:22:29,700
Sound familiar?

273
00:22:29,700 --> 00:22:30,860
Okay.

274
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:33,260
So we get, and it happens throughout all human history.

275
00:22:33,360 --> 00:22:36,980
I'm just using an example that we can like see on the news tomorrow.

276
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:39,520
But this happens throughout all human history.

277
00:22:39,520 --> 00:22:48,800
If you believe a gospel that tells you that you need to put your hope in something smaller than the slain lamb of Jesus, you will get put into a category of people.

278
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:58,680
And you and your category of people will be trying to create peace and abundance, the fruit of the true gospel, abundant life, right?

279
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,520
Your crew is looking for abundant life.

280
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:02,020
That crew is looking for abundant life.

281
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:05,680
And you're both believing a message that is in competition with one another.

282
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:18,740
So when we believe a false gospel, we are deceived and we are deceived and we are divided and peace gets removed from the earth.

283
00:23:19,620 --> 00:23:26,180
And a side consequence is the third horse, which is that of disparity.

284
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:29,200
So we've got deception, division, disparity here, the Baptist and me.

285
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,080
You guys happy with that?

286
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,040
All right, cool.

287
00:23:32,360 --> 00:23:33,980
This is so powerful.

288
00:23:33,980 --> 00:23:54,500
This image that John is showing us is that the bare necessities for life and survival become as expensive as an entire day's wage.

289
00:23:54,500 --> 00:23:59,680
A denarius is an oversimplified way of just saying a day's wage, barley and wheat.

290
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,680
These are things we have to have to survive.

291
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:08,840
John is saying when people are deceived, when they're divided into other groups and they start warring with one another,

292
00:24:09,060 --> 00:24:14,340
what happens is the bare necessities to survive become hard to come by.

293
00:24:14,340 --> 00:24:21,520
But notice the luxuries, the expensive things, the oil and the wine don't get touched at all.

294
00:24:24,220 --> 00:24:25,740
Can we connect the dots here?

295
00:24:25,740 --> 00:24:35,180
Disparity comes when we believe a false gospel, when we're divided into smaller groups of people and we start viewing each other as enemies.

296
00:24:35,180 --> 00:24:41,800
Tribes form, war and conflict happen over seemingly limited resources.

297
00:24:41,800 --> 00:24:44,580
It creates income and power disparities.

298
00:24:44,580 --> 00:24:47,460
The rich get richer and the poor barely survive.

299
00:24:47,460 --> 00:24:51,060
Can any of us think of any time in human history when this has happened?

300
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:55,280
We could be here all day giving examples, right?

301
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:59,160
I'm going to use a very common, modern example.

302
00:24:59,160 --> 00:25:06,040
This could blow up bad, but you know, you guys know I'm not afraid of risk.

303
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:08,260
It's a both-sided example.

304
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:09,020
Do you guys trust me?

305
00:25:09,020 --> 00:25:11,380
Okay, I don't know if I trust myself.

306
00:25:11,380 --> 00:25:14,160
COVID-19 happened, right?

307
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:22,020
People who have literally lived paycheck to paycheck, barely surviving, were told that they had to be forced into their homes.

308
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:23,580
They could not work.

309
00:25:23,580 --> 00:25:25,360
They could barely afford their food.

310
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:31,360
And meanwhile, what did we get images of of powerful political leaders on both sides of the aisle?

311
00:25:31,360 --> 00:25:39,920
Were they at luxurious restaurants without masks, having parties with large groups of people when they told us that we weren't allowed to go to work to get our paycheck?

312
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:43,380
Okay, this happened.

313
00:25:43,380 --> 00:25:49,280
And this happened, and this is one time it happened, and it has happened and will continue to happen.

314
00:25:49,380 --> 00:25:52,180
This is what happens when we believe false Gospels.

315
00:25:52,180 --> 00:25:56,440
Power disparity happens.

316
00:25:56,440 --> 00:26:01,920
And what, I had to be careful, because here's what happens in my heart when I give that example.

317
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:08,280
I don't know if it happens to you in your heart, but what happens to me in my heart is I immediately get furious at the politicians.

318
00:26:09,620 --> 00:26:13,520
And guess what the image John is giving us is intended to do?

319
00:26:13,520 --> 00:26:17,720
Not make you furious at image bearers of God who have believed false Gospels.

320
00:26:17,720 --> 00:26:28,900
These people in power who are benefiting from the division and disparity, who are climbing the ladder, who are all of the resources are getting hoarded at the top.

321
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:41,320
John's image is intended for us to believe and see that we do not wrestle against flesh and blood.

322
00:26:41,320 --> 00:26:46,600
We do not wrestle against the politicians on the opposite party against us.

323
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:47,800
We can disagree with them.

324
00:26:47,880 --> 00:26:50,060
We can voice our opinions, but they are not our enemies.

325
00:26:50,060 --> 00:26:52,720
They are a people to be loved.

326
00:26:52,720 --> 00:26:56,160
They are a people to be the gospel, to be proclaimed to.

327
00:26:56,160 --> 00:27:00,740
We have to watch our hearts, because the enemy of God is not people.

328
00:27:00,740 --> 00:27:02,440
It is spiritual forces.

329
00:27:02,440 --> 00:27:06,340
And that's why Revelation is giving us a peek behind the curtain to see, look at the horsemen riding.

330
00:27:06,340 --> 00:27:07,320
They are not the people.

331
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:09,700
The people have believed a false gospel.

332
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:11,440
Does that make sense?

333
00:27:12,100 --> 00:27:15,560
All right, and the end result of all of this, we've got to move on, is death.

334
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:28,800
The fourth horseman is when people are divided, when they believe false Gospels, when they fight with one another and it leads to power inequality, it's just death, war and destruction and death.

335
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:33,500
And as I studied this passage, I just have kept coming back to Romans 1 this week.

336
00:27:33,500 --> 00:27:39,240
The wrath of God is revealed when people suppress the truth for a lie.

337
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,680
This is Romans 1.

338
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:50,360
The wrath of God, and none of us like to talk about the wrath of God, but if you read Romans 1, the wrath of God is him allowing us to experience the consequences of us believing false Gospels.

339
00:27:50,360 --> 00:28:01,580
And it's him continually showing up in the midst of us believing false Gospels, inviting us to repent, inviting us to see that his way is better.

340
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:04,880
The wrath of God is revealed when people suppress the truth.

341
00:28:04,880 --> 00:28:09,700
They stop believing Jesus and they believe a false gospel, so God gives them over.

342
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:14,740
And this cycle just gets rolling down the hill and things get bad very quickly.

343
00:28:14,740 --> 00:28:22,600
God's wrath is allowing us and the world to suffer the compounding consequences of giving our allegiance to any gospel other than the gospel of Jesus.

344
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:32,280
John's images to this point are to give people a picture of what the world looks like between the inaugurated and consummated kingdom of God.

345
00:28:35,560 --> 00:28:36,260
This is heavy.

346
00:28:36,260 --> 00:28:36,500
This is heavy.

347
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:39,400
This is somewhat depressing.

348
00:28:39,400 --> 00:28:41,760
Deception, division, disparity, and death.

349
00:28:41,760 --> 00:28:42,300
And guess what?

350
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:47,220
We are not the only ones who are feeling the weight of this text.

351
00:28:47,220 --> 00:28:49,580
Which takes us to the fifth seal.

352
00:28:50,160 --> 00:28:50,980
Verse 9.

353
00:28:50,980 --> 00:28:57,840
This pattern of what the world looks like in between the inaugurated and consummated kingdom gets laid out and the next seal gets broken.

354
00:28:57,840 --> 00:29:04,880
When he opened the fifth seal, I saw under the altar the souls of those who had been slain for the word of God.

355
00:29:05,620 --> 00:29:09,100
And for the witness they had borne, they cried out with a loud voice,

356
00:29:09,100 --> 00:29:12,200
Oh, sovereign Lord, holy and true.

357
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:17,380
How long before you will judge and avenge our blood on those who dwell on the earth?

358
00:29:18,380 --> 00:29:32,320
Then they were each given a white robe and told to rest a little longer until the number of their fellow servants and their brothers should be complete who were to be killed as they themselves had been killed.

359
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:39,340
The second question these images give us an answer to is how do people respond to the brokenness of this world?

360
00:29:39,340 --> 00:29:46,680
If our world is full of deception, division, disparity, and death, how do people respond in the midst of that?

361
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:53,000
And the first of the seals after that pattern demonstrate how the church responds.

362
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:55,540
And that is they cry out, Lord, how long?

363
00:29:55,540 --> 00:29:58,220
How long will you allow this suffering?

364
00:29:58,220 --> 00:30:07,040
How long will you allow this cycle of deception that leads image bearers of God to experience the wrath of God through their own consequences and decisions?

365
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:13,580
Remember how I said each of the first four seals began with a prayer?

366
00:30:13,580 --> 00:30:17,440
The representatives of all creation cried to come.

367
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:21,280
Well, guess what happens after Romans 8 when all of creation groans?

368
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:24,480
Romans 8 says that we also groan.

369
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:26,880
The church groans.

370
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:28,200
Believers groan.

371
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:30,720
We groan so much that we don't even have words.

372
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:31,620
We read it this morning.

373
00:30:31,620 --> 00:30:37,440
The Holy Spirit has to pray for us because we don't even know what to pray in the midst of this broken world.

374
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:40,960
This is the images that we see in Revelation.

375
00:30:40,960 --> 00:30:42,540
The creation cries out.

376
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:43,140
They groan.

377
00:30:43,140 --> 00:30:43,980
Jesus, come.

378
00:30:43,980 --> 00:30:48,200
The church cries out, Lord, how long are you going to allow this to happen?

379
00:30:48,200 --> 00:30:51,880
And here is yet another reason why pastors do not like to preach the book of Revelation.

380
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:57,420
Because the answer is not what many of us would want to hear.

381
00:30:58,220 --> 00:31:07,700
Many of us in Christianity, in Christian circles, we've been given this message that the message of Jesus is just going to make our life easier and better.

382
00:31:08,800 --> 00:31:10,540
And that's not the picture we see in Revelation.

383
00:31:10,540 --> 00:31:12,380
We want comfort and blessing.

384
00:31:12,380 --> 00:31:14,260
We want to avoid suffering at all costs.

385
00:31:14,260 --> 00:31:18,900
Oftentimes, as American Christians, we aren't even comfortable talking about other people's suffering.

386
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:22,980
We'd rather just pay no attention to that thing that's happening.

387
00:31:22,980 --> 00:31:35,280
And to this day, a huge population of people are experiencing what these Christians in the fifth seal are experiencing.

388
00:31:35,280 --> 00:31:38,060
They were killed for their faith in Jesus.

389
00:31:38,060 --> 00:31:42,880
Not just killed as a secondary byproduct of a world that's broken.

390
00:31:42,980 --> 00:31:46,020
These people were killed for not rejecting Jesus.

391
00:31:46,020 --> 00:31:49,680
I got some stats to share with you from Nancy.

392
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:52,360
She's going to come up in a little bit and pray when we get to the end.

393
00:31:52,360 --> 00:31:57,360
But one in seven Christians today are persecuted worldwide.

394
00:31:57,360 --> 00:32:04,480
More than 388 million Christians suffer high levels of persecution and discrimination for their faith.

395
00:32:04,480 --> 00:32:06,500
One in five Christians are persecuted in Africa.

396
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:08,560
Two in five in Asia.

397
00:32:09,560 --> 00:32:14,860
4,849 Christians have been killed in 2026.

398
00:32:14,860 --> 00:32:16,700
4,712 detained.

399
00:32:16,700 --> 00:32:21,280
3,632 churches and Christian properties attacked.

400
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,440
The response of the martyrs is how long?

401
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:25,580
How long are you going to let this happen?

402
00:32:25,580 --> 00:32:27,540
To which Jesus replies,

403
00:32:27,540 --> 00:32:29,780
Do not worry.

404
00:32:29,780 --> 00:32:37,100
I'm about to weaponize the church against their enemies and they will avenge your death.

405
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:43,560
No, rest a little longer.

406
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:49,920
There are more of your brothers and sisters who are going to faithfully endure persecution even to the point of death.

407
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:56,000
They're going to follow the way of Jesus and they are going to be found just like you are under.

408
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:56,980
Notice where they're at.

409
00:32:56,980 --> 00:33:01,940
They're under the altar of God in heaven.

410
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:08,780
Their faithfulness, their endurance, their sacrifice is like a pleasing aroma to Jesus.

411
00:33:08,780 --> 00:33:16,960
They're offering a testimony to the true gospel in the midst of all the counterfeit Gospels that are being preached.

412
00:33:16,960 --> 00:33:23,080
Every other gospel is fighting and warring for their own success to climb up the ladder to get their own.

413
00:33:23,080 --> 00:33:34,340
And the faithful followers of the true gospel are laying down their lives as witnesses to the world that the true gospel is the only thing that leads to life.

414
00:33:34,340 --> 00:33:38,080
Now, I'm not saying we should glamorize suffering.

415
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:42,000
I'm not saying that those of us who don't experience it should long for it.

416
00:33:43,300 --> 00:33:49,620
And we also shouldn't get confused that if you're being a jerk and you're getting persecuted for it, that that means you're doing the faithful thing.

417
00:33:49,620 --> 00:33:52,380
I see that happen sometimes too.

418
00:33:52,380 --> 00:33:55,360
You being a jerk, never mind.

419
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:55,720
All right.

420
00:33:55,720 --> 00:34:01,400
I'm not saying we should long for it, but I am saying that we should be prepared for it.

421
00:34:01,600 --> 00:34:08,480
And that when we see glimpses of it in the air, that our primary response should not be just to get out of it at all costs.

422
00:34:08,480 --> 00:34:14,960
The church has been at its most healthy, faithful version of itself when it is persecuted.

423
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:23,720
Our persecuted brothers and sisters, Nancy, could give you testimony of how the church is growing and healthy and spreading in places where it's totally illegal to be a Christian.

424
00:34:23,720 --> 00:34:27,820
I'm not saying we should look for that, want that, or hope that that happens.

425
00:34:27,820 --> 00:34:37,060
But we need to realize that the way forward is not to fight back, but to keep our eyes on Jesus, who is on the throne, and prayerfully endure allegiance to the Lamb, come what may.

426
00:34:37,060 --> 00:34:40,400
The sixth seal.

427
00:34:40,400 --> 00:34:43,120
As the martyrs rest, the sixth seal is broken.

428
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:45,660
I am way behind time, so we're going to have to fly.

429
00:34:45,660 --> 00:34:46,160
Are you good?

430
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:47,420
Cool.

431
00:34:47,420 --> 00:34:54,780
The martyrs rest, the sixth seal is broken, and we see a culmination of the cycle of deception, division, disparity, and death.

432
00:34:55,300 --> 00:34:58,360
When he opened the sixth seal, I look, and behold, there was a great earthquake.

433
00:34:58,360 --> 00:35:01,280
The sun became black and sackcloth.

434
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:07,380
The full moon became like blood, and the stars of the sky fell to the earth as the fig trees sheds its winter fruit.

435
00:35:07,380 --> 00:35:12,620
The sky vanished like a scroll being rolled up, and every mountain and island was removed from its place.

436
00:35:12,620 --> 00:35:23,440
Then the kings of the earth and the great ones and the generals and the rich and the powerful and everyone, slave and free, hid themselves in caves among the rocks and from the mountains, calling to the mountains and rocks, fall on us.

437
00:35:23,440 --> 00:35:24,400
This is the sixth prayer.

438
00:35:24,400 --> 00:35:25,680
So far, we've had five prayers.

439
00:35:25,680 --> 00:35:27,640
All creation cries, Jesus, come.

440
00:35:27,640 --> 00:35:29,420
The church cries, how long?

441
00:35:29,420 --> 00:35:32,500
The people who have rejected Jesus cry, fall on us.

442
00:35:32,500 --> 00:35:35,580
Hide us from the face of him who is seated on the throne.

443
00:35:35,580 --> 00:35:41,100
From the wrath of the lamb, for the great day of their wrath has come, and who can stand?

444
00:35:41,100 --> 00:35:45,380
As the martyrs rest, the sixth seal is broken.

445
00:35:45,380 --> 00:35:47,580
The culmination of this cycle happens.

446
00:35:48,340 --> 00:35:58,720
The clash, the snowball is all the way down the hill, and even the most powerful, rich people can no longer stand the weight of the pressure.

447
00:36:01,060 --> 00:36:09,000
Those who reject the gospel of Jesus build systems and kingdoms that are at odds with one another, ultimately collapse on themselves, and no one can escape.

448
00:36:10,500 --> 00:36:13,760
And it's also interesting to me that the thing that they pray for is death.

449
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:20,480
I think as I was reading this, I heard a lot of scholars say that there's, in this text, there's almost an inherent invitation to repentance.

450
00:36:20,480 --> 00:36:24,540
They look and they see that the wrath is coming from the slain lamb.

451
00:36:25,500 --> 00:36:32,380
And there's this invitation that all it takes would be repentance, like we have, we've, we believed our own gospel, we repent, forgive us.

452
00:36:32,380 --> 00:36:39,320
They don't want to repent, they don't want forgiveness, they'd rather die believing a lie than trust the one who was slain.

453
00:36:44,900 --> 00:36:47,700
And their final prayer leads to the third question.

454
00:36:47,700 --> 00:36:50,260
Who can stand?

455
00:36:50,260 --> 00:37:02,240
Who can stand in the midst of this weight of false Gospels being believed, people groups being divided, deception, destruction, and death?

456
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:03,740
Who can stand?

457
00:37:04,460 --> 00:37:15,460
And as soon as that question is asked, John hears a number of 144,000 people from every tribe of the nation of Israel.

458
00:37:15,460 --> 00:37:18,680
And again, we don't have time to get into the weeds in this passage.

459
00:37:18,680 --> 00:37:20,840
And it has been wildly misinterpreted.

460
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:25,200
But to keep it simple, this is a common Jewish way of using numbers in a symbolic way.

461
00:37:25,200 --> 00:37:27,420
It's 12,000 people from each of the 12 tribes.

462
00:37:27,420 --> 00:37:31,980
And it starts with Judah, which is not how Jewish people listed the tribes.

463
00:37:32,980 --> 00:37:40,200
John here is saying that Israel is the fulfillment of, that Jesus is the fulfillment of what Israel was asked to do to be a blessing to all the nations.

464
00:37:40,200 --> 00:37:50,540
And he hears that all of the faithful people of Israel, the huge mass number of faithful Israelites who have walked in obedience to God, that they can stand.

465
00:37:50,540 --> 00:37:52,460
They can persevere.

466
00:37:52,460 --> 00:37:58,040
But more importantly, the vision goes on in chapter 7, just like in chapter 4 and 5.

467
00:37:58,040 --> 00:38:02,560
Remember we heard, John heard a lion, and then what did he see?

468
00:38:02,980 --> 00:38:04,080
A lamb.

469
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:10,600
In this chapter, John hears the number 144,000, 12,000 from all the 12 tribes.

470
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:16,260
And then he sees, in verse 9, after this I looked.

471
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:19,720
So I heard 144,000, 12,000 from all the tribes.

472
00:38:19,940 --> 00:38:33,780
And then I looked, and behold, a great multitude that no one could number from every nation, from all the tribes and peoples and languages, standing before the throne, before the lamb, clothed in white robes, with palm trancers in their hands, and crying out with a loud voice,

473
00:38:33,880 --> 00:38:39,220
salvation belongs to our God who sits on the throne, and to the lamb, and all of the creatures in heaven.

474
00:38:39,220 --> 00:38:46,440
Say amen, blessing, and glory, and wisdom, and thanksgiving, and honor, and power, and might be to our God forever and ever.

475
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,240
Amen.

476
00:38:47,560 --> 00:38:50,080
The answer to the question, who can stand?

477
00:38:50,080 --> 00:39:03,840
The only people that can stand through the wrath of God are the people who have bent the knee to Jesus, both Jew and Gentile, slave and free, male and female, from every language, tribe, nation, and tongue.

478
00:39:04,080 --> 00:39:13,160
If they have seen the slain lamb of Jesus as the way, and the truth, and the life, then they can stand, no matter what comes.

479
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:22,180
This is the image John wants us to meditate on, that there is a multitude of people that cannot be counted, that are persevering in the way of Jesus.

480
00:39:22,180 --> 00:39:27,860
They can stand because they've been sealed by God.

481
00:39:27,860 --> 00:39:31,600
We can stand if we've been sealed by Jesus.

482
00:39:34,080 --> 00:39:36,120
This is Romans chapter 8.

483
00:39:36,120 --> 00:39:40,620
This whole chapter 6 and chapter 7 is Romans 8.

484
00:39:40,620 --> 00:39:42,700
Romans 1 and Romans 8.

485
00:39:42,700 --> 00:39:46,060
But Romans 8 says, you got it on the slide there.

486
00:39:46,060 --> 00:39:46,360
Yeah, there.

487
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:53,800
For I am sure that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor rulers, nor things present, nor things to come, nor powers, nor height, nor depth, nor anything else,

488
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:57,760
and all of creation will be able to separate us from the love of God in Christ Jesus.

489
00:39:57,760 --> 00:39:58,680
Who can stand?

490
00:39:59,340 --> 00:40:04,720
Paul is writing to the Roman church filled with Jews and Gentiles who have bowed the knee to Jesus.

491
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:06,040
These are who can stand.

492
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:10,760
We, if we have trusted in Christ, will not be separated from the love of God.

493
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:14,620
We can stand with faithful endurance through all of the hardships of life.

494
00:40:14,620 --> 00:40:17,960
And then we get to the last seal.

495
00:40:19,860 --> 00:40:22,260
So far we've had six seals in an interlude.

496
00:40:22,260 --> 00:40:26,620
I know it's been hard to follow and I have, I'm going too fast.

497
00:40:26,620 --> 00:40:26,980
All right.

498
00:40:26,980 --> 00:40:32,600
The seventh seal breaks after the interlude of who can stand.

499
00:40:32,600 --> 00:40:35,720
And the answer is those of us who trust Jesus.

500
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:43,980
And when the Lamb opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for about half an hour.

501
00:40:44,620 --> 00:40:49,180
Then I saw the seven angels who stand before God and seven trumpets were given to them.

502
00:40:49,180 --> 00:40:52,680
And another angel came and stood at the altar with golden censer.

503
00:40:52,680 --> 00:41:01,220
And he was given much incense to offer with the prayers of all of the saints on the golden altar before the throne.

504
00:41:01,220 --> 00:41:07,160
And the smoke of the incense with the prayer of the saints rose before God from the hand of the angel.

505
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:12,800
I don't know about you, but when I was studying this, I got to the seventh seal.

506
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:15,320
I was expecting the glorious return of Jesus.

507
00:41:15,320 --> 00:41:20,400
I was expecting the wedding banquet of the Lamb.

508
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:22,860
Tears being wiped away from our eyes.

509
00:41:22,860 --> 00:41:31,180
And instead what we get is silence and the prayers of God's people rising up before the throne of God.

510
00:41:32,860 --> 00:41:39,880
If Revelation 6 is a picture of the world that we live in before Christ's kingdom is consummated,

511
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:44,580
and Revelation 7 is a picture of the people who can remain standing under pressure,

512
00:41:44,580 --> 00:41:49,620
then Revelation 8, 1 through 5, gives us instructions on how to live in the in-between.

513
00:41:49,620 --> 00:41:53,320
We do not wrestle against flesh and blood.

514
00:41:53,320 --> 00:41:57,500
Our response is not to fight our enemies or to avoid suffering at all costs.

515
00:41:57,500 --> 00:42:03,540
Our invitation is to faithfully endure with our imagination shaped by the Lamb on the throne and to pray.

516
00:42:03,540 --> 00:42:14,180
And this image of my prayers and your prayers,

517
00:42:14,180 --> 00:42:22,700
the tears in your closet for the loved ones you know that are suffering,

518
00:42:24,220 --> 00:42:28,180
for the consequences you are experiencing of living in a broken world,

519
00:42:28,180 --> 00:42:30,840
for the cancer diagnosis,

520
00:42:30,840 --> 00:42:33,440
for the unborn babies,

521
00:42:33,440 --> 00:42:38,100
all of it.

522
00:42:38,100 --> 00:42:41,300
Every tear you cry in your prayer closet

523
00:42:41,300 --> 00:42:44,040
is lifted up before the throne of God.

524
00:42:44,040 --> 00:42:47,660
And He hates it as much as you do.

525
00:42:47,660 --> 00:42:49,020
He hates it more than you do.

526
00:42:50,420 --> 00:42:53,340
And this is the image John wants us to meditate on

527
00:42:53,340 --> 00:42:57,740
as we live in this time of suffering and deception and pain and difficulty.

528
00:42:57,740 --> 00:43:00,760
The image he wants us to meditate on is our prayers

529
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:02,980
coming up before the throne of God.

530
00:43:02,980 --> 00:43:04,720
And I don't know about you,

531
00:43:04,720 --> 00:43:09,360
but far too often my prayers feel like they're hitting the top of the ceiling.

532
00:43:09,360 --> 00:43:14,440
And sometimes that causes me to not even bring them at all.

533
00:43:17,440 --> 00:43:22,780
But if we can meditate on this image of our prayers coming before the throne of God,

534
00:43:22,780 --> 00:43:26,480
what would that release in our prayer life?

535
00:43:26,480 --> 00:43:27,880
What would that invite us into?

536
00:43:27,880 --> 00:43:30,780
This whole week I've just felt like Jesus inviting me.

537
00:43:30,780 --> 00:43:31,720
It's like, I want to hear.

538
00:43:31,720 --> 00:43:35,400
I want to hear what's in there.

539
00:43:35,400 --> 00:43:38,920
I want you to lament the things that I lament.

540
00:43:38,920 --> 00:43:42,240
I want you to hope for the things that I'm hoping for.

541
00:43:42,860 --> 00:43:48,260
That your prayer is actually an active participation in my redemption plan being moved forward.

542
00:43:48,260 --> 00:43:53,660
The seven seals of revelation shape our imagination

543
00:43:53,660 --> 00:43:58,020
and anchor our hope in the slain lamb who is sitting on the throne,

544
00:43:58,020 --> 00:44:00,880
even when the future looks chaotic or unknown.

545
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:03,780
So I'm going to ask Nancy to come up.

546
00:44:04,900 --> 00:44:08,140
The visions of revelation, again, are not sheet music to be examined.

547
00:44:08,140 --> 00:44:10,140
They are a symphony to be meditated on.

548
00:44:10,140 --> 00:44:12,800
They're intended to shape our imagination

549
00:44:12,800 --> 00:44:17,660
and encourage us to prayerfully and faithfully participate in the land's kingdom.

550
00:44:17,660 --> 00:44:21,700
And I know this is heavy, and I wish that I hadn't rushed through it.

551
00:44:21,700 --> 00:44:24,840
But as I was thinking about how to conclude this service,

552
00:44:24,840 --> 00:44:27,380
the only thing that I could come up with was to have Nancy,

553
00:44:28,360 --> 00:44:33,500
a member of our church who knows personally through her ministry at OTAN,

554
00:44:33,500 --> 00:44:37,660
brothers and sisters in Christ that are currently being persecuted

555
00:44:37,660 --> 00:44:42,360
for bowing their knee to the slain lamb of Christ.

556
00:44:42,360 --> 00:44:46,500
Nancy's the media manager at OTAN to outreach to Asian nationals.

557
00:44:46,500 --> 00:44:49,820
Their mission is to train and equip persecuted Asian pastors

558
00:44:49,820 --> 00:44:52,360
to reach their people with the gospel.

559
00:44:53,360 --> 00:44:55,740
So she's going to come and share a couple of images

560
00:44:55,740 --> 00:44:59,500
and then lead us in prayer as we conclude.

561
00:44:59,500 --> 00:45:03,000
Thanks, Ryan.

562
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:03,940
Is this on?

563
00:45:03,940 --> 00:45:04,500
Can you hear me?

564
00:45:04,500 --> 00:45:05,880
It's on.

565
00:45:05,880 --> 00:45:06,540
Can you hear me?

566
00:45:06,540 --> 00:45:09,860
Is it on?

567
00:45:09,860 --> 00:45:10,360
Can you hear me?

568
00:45:10,360 --> 00:45:11,100
No.

569
00:45:11,100 --> 00:45:14,720
How about now?

570
00:45:14,720 --> 00:45:15,020
Yay.

571
00:45:15,020 --> 00:45:20,060
In 1985, a man named Otis Goodwin knew that God was calling him

572
00:45:20,060 --> 00:45:21,280
to help the church in China,

573
00:45:21,280 --> 00:45:23,300
but he really did not know what that looked like.

574
00:45:23,940 --> 00:45:26,400
So he took this exploratory trip to China.

575
00:45:26,400 --> 00:45:27,560
He had one contact,

576
00:45:27,560 --> 00:45:29,980
and at night the guy led him down a dark alley

577
00:45:29,980 --> 00:45:31,760
to a place he didn't know where he was going.

578
00:45:31,760 --> 00:45:35,020
And no sooner had he gotten inside and met two other men

579
00:45:35,020 --> 00:45:36,220
than someone knocked at the door,

580
00:45:36,220 --> 00:45:39,980
and they ushered Otis down the hall into a room under a table,

581
00:45:39,980 --> 00:45:41,420
said, be quiet, don't say anything.

582
00:45:41,420 --> 00:45:44,440
And it turned out that the man at the door was another pastor

583
00:45:44,440 --> 00:45:46,540
who stood there shaking and said,

584
00:45:46,540 --> 00:45:48,540
God told me to come to this house tonight.

585
00:45:48,540 --> 00:45:49,680
I don't know why I'm here.

586
00:45:50,260 --> 00:45:52,540
So Otis spent time with those pastors and said,

587
00:45:52,540 --> 00:45:53,360
what do you need?

588
00:45:53,360 --> 00:45:54,220
I want to help you.

589
00:45:54,220 --> 00:45:59,780
And in 1986, Otis and Roxanne founded Outreach to Asia Nationals,

590
00:45:59,780 --> 00:46:04,060
which, as Pastor Ryan said, we minister to,

591
00:46:04,060 --> 00:46:07,580
we train and equip persecuted pastors in Asia.

592
00:46:07,580 --> 00:46:09,460
We work in 13 countries.

593
00:46:09,460 --> 00:46:11,260
Two are outside of Asia.

594
00:46:11,260 --> 00:46:14,760
And believers in these countries and across the world

595
00:46:14,840 --> 00:46:17,180
live very differently than we do.

596
00:46:17,180 --> 00:46:19,920
Some are disowned by their families immediately.

597
00:46:19,920 --> 00:46:23,500
Some are kept from jobs or schools because of their faith.

598
00:46:23,500 --> 00:46:26,340
Some are followed, harassed, and threatened.

599
00:46:26,340 --> 00:46:29,660
Some have their property, including their crops, stolen.

600
00:46:29,660 --> 00:46:31,780
Some have their homes destroyed.

601
00:46:31,780 --> 00:46:33,460
They're detained and fined.

602
00:46:33,460 --> 00:46:35,840
They're imprisoned and starved.

603
00:46:35,840 --> 00:46:37,860
Some have been beaten, raped.

604
00:46:37,860 --> 00:46:39,400
Some are killed in broad daylight.

605
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:40,780
And some are never seen again.

606
00:46:41,680 --> 00:46:45,020
Some of the countries claim to allow religious freedom,

607
00:46:45,020 --> 00:46:48,700
but it's illegal to share the gospel with someone of another faith

608
00:46:48,700 --> 00:46:50,320
or someone of no faith.

609
00:46:50,320 --> 00:46:54,160
Most of our pastors work six days a week

610
00:46:54,160 --> 00:46:56,380
as farmers or manual labors,

611
00:46:56,380 --> 00:46:58,260
but their situations vary.

612
00:46:58,260 --> 00:47:00,420
I wish I could show you their faces for security.

613
00:47:00,420 --> 00:47:01,020
I can't.

614
00:47:01,020 --> 00:47:02,620
This is one of our pastors.

615
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:06,580
He and his wife moved into a village specifically to share the gospel.

616
00:47:06,580 --> 00:47:08,040
The village did not want him there.

617
00:47:08,040 --> 00:47:10,140
They're still there five years later.

618
00:47:10,140 --> 00:47:12,760
This is another of our pastors.

619
00:47:12,760 --> 00:47:14,620
This picture was taken in 2021.

620
00:47:14,620 --> 00:47:17,080
I don't know if you can see it or not, but his feet are shackled.

621
00:47:17,080 --> 00:47:20,640
He was told to close his church and stop preaching, but he didn't.

622
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:21,640
And he was put in prison.

623
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:27,200
In this particular country, family needs to bring some food to the prison

624
00:47:27,200 --> 00:47:28,540
or you're not going to get enough to eat.

625
00:47:28,860 --> 00:47:30,400
But the guards would eat his food.

626
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:32,220
This is his family.

627
00:47:32,220 --> 00:47:33,480
That's the house where he lives.

628
00:47:33,480 --> 00:47:35,060
They prayed for him while he was in prison.

629
00:47:35,060 --> 00:47:36,600
He spent eight months there.

630
00:47:36,600 --> 00:47:37,540
He was released.

631
00:47:37,540 --> 00:47:38,800
He's recovering.

632
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:42,880
This is, so that's the pastor's family.

633
00:47:42,880 --> 00:47:44,220
Yeah.

634
00:47:44,220 --> 00:47:47,280
This is one of our Southeast Asia churches meeting together.

635
00:47:47,280 --> 00:47:49,180
Again, I can't show you their faces.

636
00:47:49,180 --> 00:47:52,580
This is also one of our churches meeting on a mountaintop.

637
00:47:52,580 --> 00:47:54,920
And so is this one of our churches.

638
00:47:56,680 --> 00:48:00,240
About six months ago, one of our churches who basically had nothing but chairs,

639
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:03,080
tables, and some literature were raided by authorities.

640
00:48:03,080 --> 00:48:05,840
And they took the chairs, the tables, and the literature.

641
00:48:05,840 --> 00:48:07,820
They told them not to meet anymore.

642
00:48:07,820 --> 00:48:09,820
They'd been meeting together for over 20 years.

643
00:48:09,820 --> 00:48:13,720
They started to meet online, but in their country, that's very dangerous.

644
00:48:13,720 --> 00:48:16,060
So they met online for a while.

645
00:48:16,060 --> 00:48:18,920
They're trying to figure out how to get back together and meet in person again.

646
00:48:18,920 --> 00:48:23,960
And you can learn more about these pastors at, our website is otan.org.

647
00:48:23,960 --> 00:48:27,580
Gee, I would love it if you'd visit there, click around, read the stories.

648
00:48:27,580 --> 00:48:28,960
They're on the stories page.

649
00:48:28,960 --> 00:48:31,220
We're also on Facebook, Instagram.

650
00:48:31,220 --> 00:48:34,520
If you could share our pages with others, that's huge.

651
00:48:34,520 --> 00:48:36,760
It's free for you, and it really helps us.

652
00:48:36,760 --> 00:48:42,820
In America, our freedoms give us a buffet of resources for education.

653
00:48:42,820 --> 00:48:47,140
If we want to study to become pastors, if we just want to know the Scriptures better ourselves.

654
00:48:47,640 --> 00:48:53,280
We have colleges, universities, seminaries, online schools, seminars, certifications,

655
00:48:53,280 --> 00:48:59,520
church-based training like we do here at Canvas, unlimited print materials, and of course, Bibles.

656
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:03,280
In any shade, in any color, in any language that we want.

657
00:49:03,280 --> 00:49:08,680
Just before we pray for our brothers and sisters whose lives are very different from ours,

658
00:49:08,680 --> 00:49:11,120
I want to share this one-minute video with you.

659
00:49:11,180 --> 00:49:19,020
Now this video, I apologize, it's 15 years old, it's blurry, it's grainy, it was taken in a basement in China.

660
00:49:19,020 --> 00:49:26,480
But let me assure you that even today, when some of our brothers and sisters first have a church family,

661
00:49:26,480 --> 00:49:29,620
or get a Bible, the excitement looks like this.

662
00:49:29,620 --> 00:49:45,280
Give me Jesus, give me Jesus, give me Jesus, give me my Lord.

663
00:49:45,280 --> 00:50:15,260
Thank you.

664
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:39,780
In honor of our family members who endure daily trials for their faith, will you stand with me to pray?

665
00:50:43,340 --> 00:50:45,480
Father, thank you for the freedoms we have.

666
00:50:45,480 --> 00:50:53,520
Thank you for our church, for our pastors, for the countless opportunities and resources that we enjoy in freedom.

667
00:50:53,520 --> 00:51:01,520
Lord, we have so much when others in our family have so little, and that is hard to understand and hard to bear.

668
00:51:02,900 --> 00:51:07,820
Thank you, Lord, thank you for those you send who face extreme risk to bring the gospel to the nations,

669
00:51:07,820 --> 00:51:13,920
to let our brothers and sisters know they're not alone, they're not forgotten, they're not without family.

670
00:51:13,920 --> 00:51:16,320
The harvest is plentiful.

671
00:51:16,320 --> 00:51:22,920
Lord, send out your workers to all nations, in all languages, among all villages, among all people groups.

672
00:51:23,920 --> 00:51:32,800
Today, Lord, comfort our brothers and sisters who are afraid, who have been threatened or harmed, who have lost their leaders or their churches or their homes.

673
00:51:32,800 --> 00:51:37,440
Strengthen those whose families are suffering and whose faith is wavering.

674
00:51:37,440 --> 00:51:43,760
Help them to sense your presence right now and to regain hope and peace from you.

675
00:51:43,840 --> 00:51:49,400
Lord, comfort the pastors and leaders who fear for their families and their congregations.

676
00:51:49,400 --> 00:51:59,400
Father, when we enjoy the opportunities and resources we have, warm our hearts to remember and to lift up our brothers and sisters who have not.

677
00:51:59,400 --> 00:52:04,480
Break the strongholds of evil and power that attack your people.

678
00:52:04,480 --> 00:52:08,560
Hear the prayers of your children who are crying out to you.

679
00:52:09,240 --> 00:52:14,220
Give these men and women and their families your mercy and your protection.

680
00:52:14,220 --> 00:52:15,880
Thank you, Father.

681
00:52:15,880 --> 00:52:16,780
Amen.

682
00:52:16,780 --> 00:52:33,060
Don't like to rush moments like these, but if you don't pick up your children, Michelle will murder me.

683
00:52:36,240 --> 00:52:42,440
So, if you're, if this has stirred some things in your heart, you want to take time to go to the prayer tent or just sit in your seat quietly,

684
00:52:42,440 --> 00:52:47,160
we'll try and keep the auditorium chill zone for the next five to ten minutes.

685
00:52:47,160 --> 00:52:53,720
If you got kids, please send somebody out to get them quickly because I went too long and I apologize.

686
00:52:53,720 --> 00:52:55,600
So, go in peace, church.

687
00:52:55,600 --> 00:52:56,160
Thank you.

688
00:52:56,160 --> 00:53:03,160
Yeah.

689
00:53:03,160 --> 00:53:03,220
Yeah.

690
00:53:06,240 --> 00:53:36,220
Thank you.

691
00:53:36,240 --> 00:54:02,520
Thank you.
